From 27ed8d86d0e87684a48b1d65f91b9203b7e99106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angular Dev <dev@medpath.local>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 11:38:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(user-chip): add reusable operator identity chip with
 dropdown

- New standalone UserChipComponent (shared/components/user-chip):
  avatar + name/role trigger with an account dropdown (profile,
  settings, sign out), fully wired to UserSessionService.
- Responsive: name/role collapse below sm breakpoint, dropdown
  repositions on small screens.
- Interaction: hover/active/focus-visible states on trigger, avatar
  and menu items; chevron rotates on open; menu closes on outside
  click, Escape, or focus leaving the component.
- Two variants: 'topbar' (light pill, theme-aware) and 'sidebar'
  (dark, full-width, opens upward) reusing existing --lis-*/--text-*
  design tokens so light/dark theme switching keeps working.
- Topbar: replaced static, non-functional operator button with
  <app-user-chip variant="topbar">; dropped now-unused session
  injection.
- Sidebar footer: replaced static avatar/name/role/logout markup
  (logout icon had no handler) with <app-user-chip variant="sidebar"
  placement="up">, giving it working sign-out.
